{
  "id": "EE02Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Wound treatment",
  "description": "Wound treatment covers the full range of professional care for cuts, lacerations, and traumatic skin injuries, from thorough cleaning and tissue debridement to complex layered surgical repair. Your provider assesses the wound's depth, length, location, degree of contamination, and tissue condition to determine the appropriate level of care. The simplest cases involve irrigating and debriding the wound to remove bacteria and damaged tissue, while the most complex require multi-layer closure with advanced techniques to restore skin integrity. Local or regional anesthesia is used to keep you comfortable throughout. This type of procedure ranges in complexity from basic debridement and irrigation through to intermediate and complex repair, and the cost will vary depending on the extent of treatment required.",
